<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose slightly to 10.257 percent from 10.256 percent at the previous auction on October 22.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: May 6, 1997 (Apr 22, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.257 percent (10.256)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 545.900 milion (657.025 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 735.900 million (787.025 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.101-10.291 percent (10.101-10.289)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.101-10.600 percent (10.101-10.600)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 134 (84)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 141 (182)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds -- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
